hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"206","Abu Musa Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna narrated it, Abd Al-Ala narrated it, Saeed narrated it, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Husayn bin Al-Mundhir, Abu Bakr: He is Ibn Abi Sasan, on the authority of Al-Muhajir bin Qunfud bin Umar bin Judaan, that he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was He performed ablution, so he greeted him. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not respond until he performed ablution. Then he apologized to him and said: “I hate to mention God except “On purity” or he said: “On purity.” Al-Hasan used to take it"
